       " {'MedlineCitation': DictElement({'KeywordList': [ListElement([StringElement('Metabolic alterations', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('NAFLD', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('PCR–RFLP', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('TIMP2 gene 418 G\\u2009>\\u2009C polymorphism', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'})], attributes={'Owner': 'NOTNLM'})], 'CitationSubset': [], 'GeneralNote': [], 'OtherID': [], 'InvestigatorList': [], 'OtherAbstract': [], 'SpaceFlightMission': [], 'PMID': StringElement('42712760', attributes={'Version': '1'}), 'DateCompleted': {'Year': '2026', 'Month': '09', 'Day': '09'}, 'DateRevised': {'Year': '2026', 'Month': '09', 'Day': '10'}, 'Article': DictElement({'ArticleDate': [DictElement({'Year': '2024', 'Month': '12', 'Day': '05'}, attributes={'DateType': 'Electronic'})], 'Language': ['eng'], 'ELocationID': [StringElement('10.1007/s12291-024-01287-9', attributes={'EIdType': 'doi', 'ValidYN': 'Y'})], 'Journal': {'ISSN': StringElement('0970-1915', attributes={'IssnType': 'Print'}), 'JournalIssue': DictElement({'Volume': '41', 'Issue': '5', 'PubDate': {'Year': '2026', 'Month': 'Oct'}}, attributes={'CitedMedium': 'Print'}), 'Title': 'Indian journal of clinical biochemistry : IJCB', 'ISOAbbreviation': 'Indian J Clin Biochem'}, 'ArticleTitle': 'Tissue Inhibitor of Metalloproteinase 2 (TIMP 2) Promotor 418 G\\u2009>\\u2009C Polymorphism in Non-alcoholic Fatty Liver Disease (NAFLD) Patients of Eastern States of India.', 'Pagination': {'StartPage': '756', 'EndPage': '764', 'MedlinePgn': '756-764'}, 'Abstract': {'AbstractText': ['Tissue Inhibitor of Metalloproteinases 2 (TIMPs) prevent breakdown of extracellular matrix and is known for its role in fibrosis. The present study evaluated TIMP2 promoter site\\u2009-\\u2009418G\\u2009>\\u2009C polymorphism and risk of non-alcoholic fatty liver disease (NAFLD) in Eastern India population. In this case control study 100 clinically diagnosed NAFLD patients and 100 apparently healthy participants were enrolled and TIMP 2 Promotor (rs8179090418) G\\u2009>\\u2009C Polymorphism was studied using PCR-RFLP method with BsoBI Restriction enzyme. The association between genotypes and NAFLD risk was analyzed by odds ratio with 95% confidence interval. The frequencies of GG, GC and CC genotypes were 81%, 15% and 4% and 71%, 27% and 2% in NAFLD cases and control respectively. In dominant model, CC genotype was found to be associated with 2.05fold high risk of NAFLD (<i>p</i> value 0.046). C allele at TIMP2 promoter site -418 G\\u2009>\\u2009C when compared with G allele, odds ratio was 0.708; <i>p</i>\\u2009=\\u20090.243. A significant difference (<i>p</i>\\u2009<\\u20090.005) was found in weight, BMI, waist/ hip circumference, systolic/diastolic blood pressure, fasting plasma insulin, FPG, HbA1c, AST, ALT, GGT, total cholesterol and LDLc levels in CC genotype when compared with GG (wild type). In conclusion, TIMP2 gene Promotor (rs8179090418) 418 G\\u2009>\\u2009C polymorphism in population of Eastern states of India shows an increased risk of NAFLD in CC\\u2009+\\u2009GC genotype in comparison to wild type. TIMP2 gene 418 G\\u2009>\\u2009C polymorphism had an impact on metabolic alterations suggestive of NAFLD progression.'], 'CopyrightInformation': '© The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Association of Clinical Biochemists of India 2024. Springer Nature or its licensor (e.g. a society or other partner) holds exclusive rights to this article under a publishing agreement with the author(s) or other rightsholder(s); author self-archiving of the accepted manuscript version of this article is solely governed by the terms of such publishing agreement and applicable law.'}, 'AuthorList': ListElement([DictElement({'Identifier': [], 'AffiliationInfo': [{'Identifier': [StringElement('https://ror.org/02dwcqs71', attributes={'Source': 'ROR'}), StringElement('grid.413618.9', attributes={'Source': 'GRID'}), StringElement('0000 0004 1767 6103', a