       " {'MedlineCitation': DictElement({'KeywordList': [ListElement([StringElement('A2058 Cells', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('Apoptosis', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('Bax', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('Bcl-2', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'}), StringElement('Dacarbazine', attributes={'MajorTopicYN': 'N'})], attributes={'Owner': 'NOTNLM'})], 'CitationSubset': [], 'GeneralNote': [], 'OtherID': [], 'InvestigatorList': [], 'OtherAbstract': [], 'SpaceFlightMission': [], 'PMID': StringElement('42205222', attributes={'Version': '1'}), 'DateCompleted': {'Year': '2026', 'Month': '05', 'Day': '28'}, 'DateRevised': {'Year': '2026', 'Month': '05', 'Day': '28'}, 'Article': DictElement({'ArticleDate': [DictElement({'Year': '2024', 'Month': '08', 'Day': '16'}, attributes={'DateType': 'Electronic'})], 'Language': ['eng'], 'ELocationID': [StringElement('10.1007/s12291-024-01260-6', attributes={'EIdType': 'doi', 'ValidYN': 'Y'})], 'Journal': {'ISSN': StringElement('0970-1915', attributes={'IssnType': 'Print'}), 'JournalIssue': DictElement({'Volume': '41', 'Issue': '3', 'PubDate': {'Year': '2026', 'Month': 'Jun'}}, attributes={'CitedMedium': 'Print'}), 'Title': 'Indian journal of clinical biochemistry : IJCB', 'ISOAbbreviation': 'Indian J Clin Biochem'}, 'ArticleTitle': 'Zerumbone Induces Apoptosis and Inhibits Migration of A2058 Melanoma stem-like Cells by Producing Reactive Oxygen Species, Causing G2/M Cell Cycle Arrest, and Controlling the Expression of Genes Linked to Metastasis.', 'Pagination': {'StartPage': '403', 'EndPage': '417', 'MedlinePgn': '403-417'}, 'Abstract': {'AbstractText': ['The anticancer properties of Zerumbone, derived from the Zingiberaceae, is attracting increasing interest. Melanomas are the type of skin cancer associated with a high mortality, and current treatments have poor efficacy. This current research assesses the potential of Zerumbone to inhibit some of the malignant characteristics exhibited in the human melanoma cell line, A2058, in vitro. The Resazurin assay was used to evaluate cell viability, and wound healing assay and gelatin zymography was applied to investigate migration and MMP-2 and -\\u20099 activities. Gene expression levels associated with cell proliferation, cell differentiation, and the spread of cancer cells were measured using qRT-PCR. Apoptosis and cell cycle distribution were assessed by flow cytometry, while the generation of reactive oxygen species (ROS) inside the cells was quantified using fluorimetry. Zerumbone exhibited more cytotoxicity against melanoma cells than normal L929 and HFF cells. Zerumbone reduced the mRNA expression levels of Ki-67 and MITF while boosting NME-1. Zerumbone also caused G2/M phase arrest of the cell cycle. Zerumbone increased the ratio of Bax to Bcl-2 and the levels of p53 gene expression, inducing apoptosis in A2058 cells. Zerumbone was found to reduce the secretion and functionality of MMP-2. Zerumbone also enhanced the generation of reactive oxygen species (ROS), however, N-acetyl cysteine (NAC) reversed the ROS-induced cytotoxicity on A2058 cells. The co-administration of Zerumbone with N-acetyl cysteine (NAC) enhanced cell viability whilst reducing the generation of ROS induced by Zerumbone. Furthermore, Zerumbone enhanced the efficacy of Dacarbazine, a chemotherapeutic medication. Thus, Zerumbone has potential as a practical approach to battle melanoma, either as a standalone treatment or in conjunction with Dacarbazine. However, more pre-clinical and clinical studies are required to investigate its efficacy.'], 'CopyrightInformation': '© The Author(s), under exclusive licence to Association of Clinical Biochemists of India 2024. Springer Nature or its licensor (e.g. a society or other partner) holds exclusive rights to this article under a publishing agreement with the author(s) or other rightsholder(s); author self-archiving of the accepted manuscript version of this article is solely governed by the terms of such publishing agreement and applicable law.'}, 'AuthorList': ListElement([DictElement({'Identifier': [], 'AffiliationInfo': [{'Identifier': [StringElement('https://ror.org/00bvysh61', attributes={'Source': 'ROR'}), StringElement('grid.411768.d', attributes={'Source': 'GRID'}), StringElement('0000 0004 1756 1744', attributes={'Source': 'ISNI'})], 'Affiliation': 'Faculty of Paramedical, Mashhad Branch, Islamic Azad University, Mashhad, Iran.'}], 'LastName': 'Ostadi', 'ForeName': 'Atieh', 'Initials': 'A'}, attributes={'ValidYN': 'Y', 'EqualContrib': 'Y'}), DictElement({'Identifier': [], 'AffiliationInfo': [{'Identifier': [StringElement('https://ror.org/03r42d171', attributes={'Source': 'ROR'}), StringElement('grid.488433.0', attributes={'Source': 'GRID'}), StringElement('0000 0004 0612 8339', attributes={'Source': 'ISNI'})], 'Affiliation': 'Department of Pharmacology, Faculty of Medicine, Zahedan University of Medical Sciences, Zahedan, Iran.'}], 'LastName': 'Vahedi', 'ForeName': 'Mohammad Mahdi', 'Initials': 'MM'}, attributes={'ValidYN': 'Y', 'EqualContrib': 'Y'}), DictElement({'Identifier': [], 'AffiliationInfo': [{'Identifier': [StringElement('https://ror.org/04sfka033', attributes={'Source': 'ROR'}), StringElement('grid.411583.a', attributes={'Source': 'GRID'}), StringElement('0000 0001 2198 6209', attributes={'Source': 'ISNI'})], 'Affiliation': 'Department of Medical Biochemistry, Faculty of Medicine, Mashhad University of Medical Sciences, Mashhad, Iran.'}], 'LastName': 'Abbasinezhad-Moud', 'ForeName': 'Farzaneh', 'Initials': 'F'}, attributes={'ValidYN': 'Y'}), DictElement({'Identifier': [], 'AffiliationInfo': [{'Identifier': [StringElement('https://ror.org/03r42d171', attributes={'Source': 'ROR'}), StringElement('grid.488433.0', attributes={'Source': 'GRID'}), StringElement('0000 0004 0612 8339', attributes={'Source': 'ISNI'})], 'Affiliation': 'Faculty of Medicine, Zahedan University of Medical Sciences, Sistan and Baluchestan Province,